summary:
The change passes: the design does what the request asked, and all nine criteria are met. It adds docs/design/scope-guard.md, a proposed D127 in docs/decisions.md and a CHANGELOG line, and touches nothing outside those three files. The design covers:
- the value-versus-cost test with sourced inputs and a decision table;
- the request's figures, each labeled as supplied by the request;
- five thrash signals, all with numbers, replayed on the named cases (the same-criterion signal fires on the speedup after the second rejection);
- which parts rules decide and which a model scores, and what a model verdict may not override;
- the guard's powers, with Sri reached through the existing steward channel;
- protection for learnings work (a quota, proceed on doubt, and an appeal);
- its relation to the steward, Hestia and the keep rule;
- the Artemis/Demeter mapping, confirmed against the BRIEF.md pantheon table;
- a 10-job build plan ordered by dependency.

I checked its repository citations against the files: BRIEF.md lines 603-607 and 1067, job-planning.md section 9 ($1.67 and $2.50), roles-and-ladder.md, and D125/D126. All match. Athena's test record passed with 1251 tests. Athena skipped fmt because the change is docs only, so I ran `cargo fmt --all --check` myself and it passed. One minor gap is worth fixing later: the decision table gives no outcome for cheap work with a value score of 0.
